WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:08.251
Liquid AI's new reasoning model targets local agents.

2
00:00:08.351 --> 00:00:13.252
Its name highlights active compute, but that is only
one part of deployment.

3
00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:20.495
The model has twenty-four billion parameters, with
about two point four five billion active per token.

4
00:00:20.595 --> 00:00:24.749
The Q-four weight file alone is fourteen point five
gigabytes.

5
00:00:24.849 --> 00:00:27.255
Runtime memory needs more room.

6
00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:31.465
Liquid reports fast decoding on an M-five Max.

7
00:00:31.565 --> 00:00:36.359
Its much larger B-three-hundred number combines many
concurrent requests.

8
00:00:36.459 --> 00:00:39.269
Neither number is the time to finish your task.

9
00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:41.844
The published results are mixed.

10
00:00:41.944 --> 00:00:47.517
Liquid reports stronger tool-task scores than Qwen in
some tests, but lower coding scores.

11
00:00:47.617 --> 00:00:51.195
These are vendor measurements, not independent
confirmation.

12
00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:54.975
A local model still needs an agent harness.

13
00:00:55.075 --> 00:00:58.716
That software controls tools, permissions, and
recovery.

14
00:00:58.816 --> 00:01:02.224
External search can still send data off the device.

15
00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:07.895
Choose by available memory, your actual tasks, and
acceptable delay.

16
00:01:07.995 --> 00:01:10.976
Check the model license before commercial use.

17
00:01:11.076 --> 00:01:16.596
Fast token generation is useful when the whole system
delivers the right result.

